    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1244">

                <pb facs="1016" n="1006" xml:id="pg1006"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00B/11–949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Peiping</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-09T15:00:00+08:00">November 9, 1949—3
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 9—4:16 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1954. ReDeptel 778, November 8.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d1244-f1"/> Agree re
                    desirability releasing at this time text letter November 3 to Chou En-lai.</p>
                <p>Letter still unacknowledged and no answer from Foreign Office to my letter of
                    October 31 requesting interview.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1244-f1" n="54" xml:id="d1244-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it stated: “Dept will release text ur Nov 3 ltr to Chou En-lai at
                    press conference Nov 9.” (893.00B/11–849) See press release of November 10,
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, November 21, 1949, p.
                    759.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
